SUMMARY:ABCD Reads Yesteryear by Caro Claire Burke
DESCRIPTION:A Book Club\, Downtown (ABCD)\nABCD Reads ***Yesteryear*** by 
 Caro Claire Burke.\n([RESULTS](https://opavote.com/results/484928177229004
 8) of the poll for this event.)\n\n**:: ABOUT THE BOOK ::**\n"A traditiona
 l American woman\, a beautiful wife and mother who sells her pioneer lifes
 tyle of raw milk and farm-fresh eggs to her millions of social media follo
 wers\, suddenly awakens cold\, filthy\, and terrified in the brutal realit
 y of 1855—where she must unravel whether this living nightmare is an ela
 borate hoax\, a twisted reality show\, or something far more sinister." (f
 rom [BookMarks](https://bookmarks.reviews/reviews/yesteryear/))\n\n"The ch
 asm between social media and reality runs deep and dark in Caro Claire Bur
 ke’s debut novel\, “Yesteryear\,” which crawls into the psyche of a 
 tradwife influencer so maddening and mesmerizing that Anne Hathaway has al
 ready signed on to play her in the movie adaptation.\n“Sometimes it actu
 ally made me sick\,” Natalie Heller Mills narrates\, “how perfect my l
 ife was\, and how good I was at living it.” Note her use of the past ten
 se." (from [New York Times Book Review](https://archive.ph/WHSQ6#selection
 -753.0-764.0))\n\n**:: ABOUT THE EVENT ::**\nYou are welcome to arrive 30 
 minutes before the event and stay 30 minutes or longer afterward to connec
 t with other attendees outside the book talk.\n\nPlease ensure you have re
 ad the book before attending (though finishing any book is not a barrier t
 o participating\, as long as you don't mind spoilers).\n\nFirst-time atten
 dees can join for free. If the event is full\, we maintain an unofficial w
 aitlist. Please send [Michael](https://www.meetup.com/members/55295192/) a
  direct message for more information\, in either case.\n\nWe request a $3 
 contribution from regular attendees to help cover our monthly meetup costs
 .\n\n**:: ABOUT OUR NEXT BOOK ::**\nAt the end of each event\, we will ask
  for nominees for our next book. If you have a good one in mind\, please e
 nsure it is between 200-400 pages long\, available from the Toronto Public
  Library\, and counts as contemporary literary fiction (though these are n
 ot hard and fast rules). When enough nominees are collected\, Michael will
  send the members a direct message with a link where you can vote.
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/a-book-club-downtown-abcd/events/3166
 09319/
