SUMMARY:ABCD Reads American Hagwon by Min Jin Lee
DESCRIPTION:A Book Club\, Downtown (ABCD)\nABCD Reads [American Hagwon](ht
 tps://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/record/S234C4792135) by Min Jin Lee (author
  of [Pachinko](https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/record/S234C3448477))\n([R
 ESULTS](https://opavote.com/results/6718256866656256) of the poll for this
  event.)\n\n**:: ABOUT THE BOOK ::**\n"In schools and churches\, hotel roo
 ms and nail salons\, law firms and fried-fish shops\; in cramped\, dingy a
 partments and luxury\, gated communities\, the men\, women\, and children 
 in American Hagwon struggle to find satisfaction and meaning in a world th
 at seems to grow less forgiving with each passing year. Once comfortably m
 iddle class in Korea\, John and Helen Koh and their three children\, Bo\, 
 DH\, and Mido\, find their lives upended\, first by a shocking betrayal by
  John's oldest friend\, then by the 1997 Asian financial crisis." (from [B
 ookMarks](https://bookmarks.reviews/reviews/american-hagwon/))\n\n"At last
 \, the National Book Award finalist and NYT bestselling author of Pachinko
  returns with a breathtaking contemporary epic: Min Jin Lee has written a 
 masterpiece by turns sweeping and intimate\, one that reckons with ambitio
 n and moderation\, lust and loyalty\, personal dreams and familial duty." 
 (from [Goodreads](https://www.goodreads.com/en/book/show/245886309-america
 n-hagwon))\n\n**:: ABOUT THE EVENT ::**\nYou are welcome to arrive 30 minu
 tes before the event and stay 30 minutes or longer afterward to connect wi
 th other attendees outside the book talk.\n\nPlease ensure you have read t
 he book before attending (though finishing any book is not a barrier to pa
 rticipating\, as long as you don't mind spoilers).\n\nFirst-time attendees
  can join for free. If the event is full\, we maintain an unofficial waitl
 ist. Please send [Michael](https://www.meetup.com/members/55295192/) a dir
 ect message for more information\, in either case.\n\nWe request a $3 cont
 ribution from regular attendees to help cover our monthly meetup costs.\n\
 n**:: ABOUT OUR NEXT BOOK ::**\nAt the end of each event\, we will ask for
  nominees for our next book. If you have a good one in mind\, please ensur
 e it is between 200-400 pages long\, available from the Toronto Public Lib
 rary\, and counts as contemporary literary fiction (though these are not h
 ard and fast rules). When enough nominees are collected\, Michael will sen
 d the members a direct message with a link where you can vote.
