SUMMARY:ABCD Reads The End of Everything by M. John Harrison
DESCRIPTION:A Book Club\, Downtown (ABCD)\nABCD Reads [The End of Everythi
 ng](https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/record/S234C4802129) by M. John Harri
 son\, winner of the [2026 Booker Prize](https://thebookerprizes.com/the-bo
 oker-library/prize-years/2026).\n\n([RESULTS](https://opavote.com/results/
 6285142977675264) of the poll for this event.)\n\n**:: ABOUT THE BOOK ::**
 \n"Phillip Tennent makes his living at the tideline\, collecting artifacts
  that wash up from the Channel. It's been years since the crisis changed e
 verything\, but its exact nature remains obscure. Government barely functi
 ons\, the seas are full of new creatures\, an entire continent has been mi
 slaid. It feels like the end. Now Phillip has fished out of the water an o
 bject he can't keep. A creature that keeps changing. An artifact he must t
 ake inland\, before it destroys everything he thinks he knows." (from [Boo
 kMarks](https://bookmarks.reviews/reviews/the-end-of-everything/))\n\n"The
  End of Everything is a slyly satirical and unsettling post-apocalyptic ad
 venture into the limits of human understanding from the peerless master of
  contemporary fiction." (from [Goodreads](https://www.goodreads.com/en/boo
 k/show/245886309-american-hagwon))\n\n**:: ABOUT THE EVENT ::**\nYou are w
 elcome to arrive 30 minutes before the event and stay 30 minutes or longer
  afterward to connect with other attendees outside the book talk.\n\nPleas
 e ensure you have read the book before attending (though finishing any boo
 k is not a barrier to participating\, as long as you don't mind spoilers).
 \n\nFirst-time attendees can join for free. If the event is full\, we main
 tain an unofficial waitlist. Please send [Michael](https://www.meetup.com/
 members/55295192/) a direct message for more information\, in either case.
 \n\nWe request a $3 contribution from regular attendees to help cover our 
 monthly meetup costs.\n\n**:: ABOUT OUR NEXT BOOK ::**\nAt the end of each
  event\, we will ask for nominees for our next book. If you have a good on
 e in mind\, please ensure it is between 200-400 pages long\, available fro
 m the Toronto Public Library\, and counts as contemporary literary fiction
  (though these are not hard and fast rules). When enough nominees are coll
 ected\, Michael will send the members a direct message with a link where y
 ou can vote.
